<!--
  BlockML Core — package reference value type (package string, no type segment)

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.type.PackageReference
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <name>PackageReference</name>
  <type>type:PackageReference</type>
  <baseType>type:PackageIdentifier</baseType>
  <is>A Block package name reference</is>

  <documentation>
    ValueType for package references — reverse-domain package strings without a type (class)
    segment that must be known in the corpus. Extends PackageIdentifier (syntax) with existence.
    Unqualified name PackageReference resolves to org.blockml.bml.type.PackageReference.
    Sibling of TypeReference under Text — not a TypeReference subtype. No generic parameters.

    Package format (Java-style reverse-domain, dot-separated, all lowercase):
    • Package segments — lowercase (for example org.blockml.bml.core, com.machineblocks.bml.type)
    • No class segment — PascalCase type names belong on TypeReference (org.blockml.bml.type.Integer
      is a type FQN, not a package)
    • Valid: org.blockml.bml.type · com.example.bml
    • Invalid as PackageReference: org.blockml.bml.type.Integer · core:Block · Integer

    Namespace prefixes in BML (core:, type:, def:, …) bind to packages; a prefix that targets a
    Package resolves to that package string (core → org.blockml.bml.core). A prefix that targets an
    Annotation is not a PackageReference.

    Primary use — documentation see package= on StructuralDefinition.Reference, and any property
    that names a package rather than a Block type. When a package reference must appear as an Entity
    in composition or aggregation, use org.blockml.bml.type.PackageReferenceEntity.

    A package name that need not exist uses PackageIdentifier — not PackageReference. Block type
    FQNs and TypeExpressions use org.blockml.bml.type.TypeReference — not PackageReference.
    Instance pointers use InstanceReference. Member definition paths use the MemberIdentifier
    branch.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:BmlNamespace" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Package vs Annotation xmlns targets and domain.bml.* layout.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:TypeIdentityDerivation" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Namespace resolution — packages vs type FQNs.
    </see>
    <see type="type:PackageIdentifier" relation="SeeAlso">
      Parent ValueType — package-string syntax without existence.
    </see>
    <see type="type:TypeReference" relation="ContrastsWith">
      Sibling ValueType for Block type FQNs / TypeExpressions — includes the class segment.
    </see>
    <see type="def:StructuralDefinition" relation="SeeAlso">
      see package attribute typed as PackageReference.
    </see>
    <see type="type:PackageReferenceEntity" relation="SeeAlso">
      Entity wrapper for PackageReference values in composition or aggregation.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
